learnings:
  - 'The double-tilde aspect bug''s TRUE root was premise/core/src/aggregator.ts:147 (symbol: `~${id}` over an already-''~''-prefixed .purpose key), upstream of the aspect-graph DB layer the original report named — fixing the builder corrects ALL consumers (db, navigator, search, aspect_check) at once; the DB-layer canonicalize+dedup is defense-in-depth that also folds aspects declared both bare and prefixed.'
  - Collapsing doubled aspect ids surfaced a hidden UNIQUE-constraint collision (same aspect declared bare AND '~'-prefixed across files) that materializeAspects' catch{} was silently swallowing — any id-merging fix MUST dedupe, not just transform.
  - 'The f:N collision fix uses a U+001F (unit-separator) sentinel prefix on the slot token: literal payloads go through JSON.stringify which escapes all control chars, so the sentinel is unforgeable by string content — keeping the readable ''f:N'' after it preserves existing toContain(''f:0'') assertions and debug dumps.'
  - A long-running MCP server caches its aggregation/aspect-graph at session start; an on-disk reindex via fresh code (CLI/tsx) corrects the data, but the server's tools stay stale until restart — verify framework-data fixes on-disk (sqlite3 + in-process getAspect), not only through the live MCP tool.
